' 4+1 process view - Set the new password (US05) · a single response for any bad link; everything in one transaction
' Version 1.1 - 2026-11-10
' For: whoever writes code and whoever debugs.
' Documented decision: A single 400 response for any bad link; the new password, the session revocation and the email in one transaction (US05).
' Not drawn: internal detail of the classes; refusals that do not change the sequence (they are in the text of process.md).
@startuml process-reset-confirm
!include ../style.puml

title Process view - set the new password (US05): a single response for any bad link; everything in one transaction
autonumber

participant "Accounts" as WEB_F_AUTH
box "ASP.NET Core API"
  participant "Accounts and sessions" as API_AUTH
  participant "Recovery" as API_AUTH_RESET
  participant "Data Protection" as CC_DATAPROT
end box
database "PostgreSQL" as C_DB

WEB_F_AUTH -> API_AUTH : POST /api/auth/password-reset/confirm { email, token,\nnewPassword } [email and token read from the address;\n[AllowAnonymous], per-IP limit]
API_AUTH -> API_AUTH_RESET : ConfirmAsync
API_AUTH_RESET -> API_AUTH_RESET : Validates newPassword (400 on the field); empty email or token → 400\ninvalid_or_expired_reset_link
API_AUTH_RESET -> C_DB : FindByEmailAsync and eligibility (active Player or Owner) [SELECT\nusers]
group Transaction
  API_AUTH_RESET -> CC_DATAPROT : UserManager.ResetPasswordAsync(user, token, newPassword)
  CC_DATAPROT -> C_DB : Validates purpose, lifetime (system clock) and security\nstamp [SELECT data_protection_keys]
  alt wrong, expired or already used token
    API_AUTH_RESET -> C_DB : ROLLBACK [SQL]
    API_AUTH --> WEB_F_AUTH : 400 invalid_or_expired_reset_link (the same for an unknown\naccount)
  else valid
    API_AUTH_RESET -> C_DB : New hash and new security stamp: this token and earlier ones\nstop working [UPDATE users]
    API_AUTH_RESET -> C_DB : Revokes all sessions [UPDATE refresh_tokens SET revoked_at]
    API_AUTH_RESET -> C_DB : ResetAccessFailedCountAsync, SetLockoutEndDateAsync(null)\n[UPDATE users]
    API_AUTH_RESET -> C_DB : INSERT outbox_messages (password_changed); COMMIT [SQL]
    API_AUTH --> WEB_F_AUTH : 204; nobody ends up signed in
  end
end
@enduml
